  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1205 PM CDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\nA front will be kinda/sorta near us to our north, but offer \nlittle real impact here as high pressure reorients and \nreinforces its grip upon us within the next 48-72 hours. H5 \nheights here around 588 DM now will see a 595 DM anticyclone \ncenter over the lower half of the MS Valley by the end of the \nweekend, then translate overhead upon its migration to the TN \nValley by mid week. Until then, the trailing end of a \nsagging/nearby front (to the north/west) may offer just enough \nconvergent forcing to yield a 10-20% chance of a shower or \nstorm, mainly on our CWA periphery, before it is effectively \npinched off by the building High(s). \n\nAfter that, it's all high pressure and its impacts, which is\nmoving us AGAIN toward headline heat during the Tue-Thu time frame.\nA nose of 25C H8 temps ridges across the CWA with the \ntranslation of the High, with resultant max temps pushing the \nmid 90s again. Return flow dew points around 70F/into the lower\n70s will make for HI's pushing 100F/into the lower 100s each \nday.\n\nSome relief may be noted toward the week's end, as the high\npressure ridge is in turn pinched off by approaching low\npressure from the north and west as well as the south and east,\nso its slow/steady retreat effectively falls heights here and\nallows for the potential for small pcpn chances to make a \ngradual return to the forecast.",
